Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: initialize phone charge units

SM8350-class firmware supplies charge-domain values but has no
BATTMGR_BAT_INFO response to initialize unit. The zero-initialized mWh
value causes valid CHARGE_FULL and CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN reads to fail with
ENODATA. Set the unit before registering the phone battery. Leave laptop
firmware-selected units, charging controls and reported values unchanged.

Based on Jan-Michael Brummer's independently published 2026-08-29 patch:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2608.3/10893.html
Local backport only: upstream merge and ROG5 hardware validation
are not established here. Linux driver license: GPL-2.0-only.

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index da0728dd663ae1063a0b020b352e02f45574fb88..22038b0aa3fcd8d25026924b4a1bfecfe5249071 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1867,6 +1867,9 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_probe(struct auxiliary_device *adev,
 			return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(battmgr->wls_psy),
 					     "failed to register wireless charing power supply\n");
 	} else {
+		/* Phone firmware reports charge units without BATTMGR_BAT_INFO. */
+		battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh;
+
 		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550)
 			psy_desc = &sm8550_bat_psy_desc;
 		else
